\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs32\b\cf1 Paratext plugins\cf0\b0\fs22\par
Plugins for Paratext 9, written for Bible translation teams. Each one adds an item to the Tools menu of a project's text window. To install plugins: download Install_Phils_tools.exe, close Paratext, run it, tick the plugins and click Install.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Parallel Passages Editor\b0  \endash  version 1.2\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Parallel Passages Editor...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Hides or shows books and chapters in Paratext's list of parallel passages (ParallelPassages.xml), so that the Parallel Passages tool shows only the passages your project needs. The first save keeps a copy of the original file. A project's hidden list can be saved and applied again after a Paratext update. The editor runs as administrator, because the list is in the Paratext program folder.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 AutoCorrect Editor\b0  \endash  version 1.1\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > AutoCorrect Editor...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Edits the project's autocorrect.txt, the rules Paratext uses to replace what you type, in a table instead of a text file. A character browser helps you enter any Unicode character. If the project has no autocorrect.txt yet, saving creates it.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Custom Versification Editor\b0  \endash  version 1.0\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Custom Versification Editor...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Edits the project's custom.vrs: the chapters and verse counts that differ from the project's versification, verse mappings, and missing verses. If the project has no custom.vrs yet, saving creates it.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Custom Stylesheet Editor\b0  \endash  version 1.0\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Custom Stylesheet Editor...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Edits the project's custom.sty. Each marker shows the value from the project's stylesheet beside your change, and you can add new markers. Lines you do not change are kept exactly as they were, and changes follow the rules Paratext uses to read stylesheets.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Numbered Markers\b0  \endash  version 1.7\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Numbered Markers...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Lists the markers the project uses both with and without a number (such as \\mt beside \\mt1) and changes the ones you tick to a single form. It changes only the chapters you are allowed to edit, after making a Paratext history point and a backup.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Marker Spaces\b0  \endash  version 1.3\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Marker Spaces...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Finds missing or extra spaces around USFM markers and fixes the ones you tick. Each problem is shown as it is now and as it will be after the fix; double-click a row to go to the place in Paratext. It changes only the chapters you are allowed to edit, after making a history point and a backup.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Numbered Book Titles\b0  \endash  version 1.1\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Numbered Book Titles...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Checks how the numbered books (1 Samuel, 2 Kings, 1-3 John...) write their number in \\h, \\toc1-3, \\mt and the book names, lists the books that differ from the usual style, and changes the lines you tick. Book names are only reported: change them in Paratext's book name settings.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Special Features\b0  \endash  version 1.7\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Special Features...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Lists the places where published Bibles often use special formatting (lists, letters, inscriptions, Old Testament quotations...) and shows whether your project formats them, leaves them plain or has not drafted them yet. You can add your own places and share them. It does not change the text.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Project Settings Report\b0  \endash  version 2.5\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Project Settings Report...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Shows the project's settings (Settings.xml and the language settings) as a web page, with a description of each setting. Valid characters and punctuation are shown with how often the text uses them, along with the characters and punctuation found in the text that are not in the lists. It does not change anything.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Style Guide\b0  \endash  version 1.16\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Style Guide...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Fills in Biblica's style-guide modules (Punctuation, Footnotes, Headings, Poetry, Quotations and more) with suggested answers drawn from the project's text, which the team reviews and exports to Word. Answers are saved only on your computer. English only for now.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Send Notes to Project\b0  \endash  version 1.3\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Send Notes to Project...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Sends notes written in a consultant notes project to the project they are about: tick the notes of a chapter, choose which comment of each note to send, and each becomes a new note at the same verse in the project you choose (remembered until you change it). "Sent to ..." is added to the original note, so nothing is sent twice by mistake.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Bulk Note Editing (experimental)\b0  \endash  version 1.6\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Bulk Note Editing...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Lists the notes of a verse, a chapter, a book or the whole project, of one or several projects, filtered by status, read or unread, who wrote them, who commented, who they are assigned to, date, words or tag, and resolves, assigns or marks as read or unread the notes you tick, all at once. Resolving or assigning adds a comment, so the notes' history stays complete. Notes cannot be deleted: Paratext does not let plugins do that.\par
\pard\keepn\sb240\sa60\sl276\slmult1\fs26\b\cf1 Phils Custom (cms) Checks\b0  \endash  version 1.5\cf0\fs22\par
\pard\keepn\sa60\sl276\slmult1\i\cf2 Menu: Tools > Phils Custom (cms) Checks...\cf0\i0\par
\pard\sa120\sl276\slmult1 Lists Phil's custom checks (titles, section headings, quotation marks, footnotes, figures, marker spaces, capitals and more, in English or Spanish) and runs the one you choose through Paratext's own check window, so the results appear in Paratext's list as usual. The checks come with the plugin: nothing has to be copied into the cms folder.\par
\pard\sb360\sl276\slmult1\fs18\cf2 List updated November 13, 2026\cf0\fs22\par
